00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:01,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:01,185 --> 00:00:04,465
Do you remember the legend of the tree
that proves true love?

2
00:00:04,545 --> 00:00:06,665
If a couple kisses under this tree
and they're meant for each other,

3
00:00:06,745 --> 00:00:08,705
they will stay together.

4
00:00:08,785 --> 00:00:11,345
After the kiss,
whether we feel something or nothing,

5
00:00:11,425 --> 00:00:13,225
we both have to say it honestly.

6
00:00:13,305 --> 00:00:15,785
One. Two. Three.

7
00:00:15,865 --> 00:00:17,185
-I felt something.
-I felt something.

8
00:00:59,465 --> 00:01:00,345
Are you awake?

9
00:01:07,625 --> 00:01:09,625
How are you feeling? Tired?

10
00:01:10,305 --> 00:01:11,825
I'm still a little wiped out.

11
00:01:12,385 --> 00:01:13,985
My legs ache too.

12
00:01:17,265 --> 00:01:18,745
Of course you're exhausted.

13
00:01:18,825 --> 00:01:21,265
You got lost in the woods last night.

14
00:01:23,305 --> 00:01:26,625
Go take a shower.
They'll probably gather everyone soon.

15
00:01:26,705 --> 00:01:28,185
I'll pack your things for you.

16
00:01:38,185 --> 00:01:39,985
Do you really have to do all this?

17
00:01:40,065 --> 00:01:41,905
Do what?

18
00:01:42,705 --> 00:01:47,905
I'm just acting like someone
you've allowed to win you over.

19
00:01:51,545 --> 00:01:55,105
Last night, I made you
lose your way in the woods.

20
00:01:59,545 --> 00:02:00,985
This time…

21
00:02:03,985 --> 00:02:05,545
I'll make you fall for me.

22
00:02:14,665 --> 00:02:16,105
Fall for you, my ass!

23
00:02:17,705 --> 00:02:19,105
I'm going to take a shower.

24
00:02:58,105 --> 00:02:59,185
How are you feeling?

25
00:03:00,505 --> 00:03:05,185
Did you and I…

26
00:03:09,345 --> 00:03:10,425
I thought I was dreaming.

27
00:03:12,265 --> 00:03:13,745
I thought it was a dream.

28
00:03:13,825 --> 00:03:15,425
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to do it.

29
00:03:16,225 --> 00:03:19,345
I shouldn't have done that to you
while I was drunk.

30
00:03:21,745 --> 00:03:23,745
Fine. Just forget it.

31
00:03:24,505 --> 00:03:26,105
Don't overthink it.

32
00:03:26,185 --> 00:03:27,825
Consider it…

33
00:03:29,145 --> 00:03:30,545
a one-night stand.

34
00:03:32,825 --> 00:03:35,265
I won't say anything,
and you won't either.

35
00:03:35,345 --> 00:03:36,305
That's all.

36
00:03:38,905 --> 00:03:40,985
-Well…
-Don't overthink it.

37
00:03:41,505 --> 00:03:45,185
What we have is just a situationship.

38
00:04:16,305 --> 00:04:17,305
Will you be my boyfriend?

39
00:04:17,384 --> 00:04:19,985
-Yeah.
-Really?

40
00:04:33,945 --> 00:04:35,705
I will never be like you, Rin.

41
00:05:50,065 --> 00:05:51,145
Hey!

42
00:05:59,345 --> 00:06:02,825
About everyone
searching for you last night…

43
00:06:03,625 --> 00:06:05,425
You weren't acting, were you?

44
00:06:06,705 --> 00:06:10,145
Not everyone sees everything
as content as you do.

45
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:13,705
What's really going on between
you and Khobfa? What about Krit?

46
00:06:13,785 --> 00:06:16,385
-You flirted with Krit to get his help.
-I didn't.

47
00:06:16,905 --> 00:06:20,025
If you're sure you don't like him,
then end things cleanly.

48
00:06:21,065 --> 00:06:22,665
I've already cut him off.

49
00:06:24,905 --> 00:06:27,665
But can your guy do the same?

50
00:06:28,865 --> 00:06:31,825
I know you can cut people off.
You're good at it.

51
00:06:32,745 --> 00:06:35,825
You cut off your entire group
of close friends before.

52
00:06:38,905 --> 00:06:41,225
I'm ready. Are you?

53
00:06:43,385 --> 00:06:44,545
Rin.

54
00:06:45,265 --> 00:06:47,065
Are you done? Shall we go now?

55
00:06:49,505 --> 00:06:50,585
-Hold on!
-Hold on!

56
00:06:54,145 --> 00:06:56,905
Here we go.
We even got the sea in the shot.

57
00:06:58,025 --> 00:06:59,185
Smile.

58
00:07:16,825 --> 00:07:18,185
Should I carry that for you?

59
00:07:40,345 --> 00:07:42,785
So Rin, what's the deal with you two?

60
00:07:43,625 --> 00:07:46,105
You two are acting weird.

61
00:07:46,185 --> 00:07:48,505
You've defined your relationship,
haven't you?

62
00:07:49,185 --> 00:07:50,345
No.

63
00:07:51,265 --> 00:07:53,345
Khobfa just asked if he could win me over.

64
00:07:54,585 --> 00:07:56,025
Seriously?

65
00:07:56,105 --> 00:07:57,825
Are you pulling tricks on him again?

66
00:07:57,905 --> 00:07:58,945
Exactly.

67
00:07:59,025 --> 00:08:01,745
Jeez. Why would I?

68
00:08:01,825 --> 00:08:04,065
-We already kissed.
-What?

69
00:08:09,265 --> 00:08:10,265
Well…

70
00:08:10,345 --> 00:08:13,705
I guess the True Love Tree
really does work.

71
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:15,025
-Yeah.
-It's holy, right?

72
00:08:15,105 --> 00:08:17,065
-It really is. Awesome.
-Yeah.

73
00:08:17,145 --> 00:08:19,145
-Come on, let's go!
-That was hard.

74
00:08:19,225 --> 00:08:20,825
-He's shy.
-Shy, huh? Come on.

75
00:08:21,425 --> 00:08:24,425
-Hey, can I hold it too?
-Let me hold your hand too!

76
00:08:36,105 --> 00:08:38,105
Is the AC blowing on you?

77
00:08:54,665 --> 00:08:55,705
Hey.

78
00:08:58,305 --> 00:08:59,345
About last night…

79
00:08:59,425 --> 00:09:01,705
-I…
-What song did you send me?

80
00:09:07,145 --> 00:09:09,985
I listened to it and thought of you,

81
00:09:10,065 --> 00:09:11,345
so I shared it with you.

82
00:09:15,225 --> 00:09:16,345
Here, give it a listen.

83
00:09:24,785 --> 00:09:26,465
I'm going to rest my eyes.

84
00:09:27,305 --> 00:09:28,705
I barely slept last night.

85
00:09:29,785 --> 00:09:32,305
I'll listen to it when I wake up.

86
00:09:34,945 --> 00:09:35,825
Okay.

87
00:10:08,265 --> 00:10:09,585
Wow!

88
00:10:11,225 --> 00:10:15,825
Khobfa, order whatever you want.

89
00:10:15,905 --> 00:10:17,145
This meal is on us.

90
00:10:17,225 --> 00:10:20,465
Yeah. Consider it our way of thanking you

91
00:10:20,545 --> 00:10:23,985
for keeping our beloved friend safe.

92
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:28,825
Come to think of it,

93
00:10:28,905 --> 00:10:32,225
this is the first time
we've really gotten to talk to you.

94
00:10:32,305 --> 00:10:35,145
We'd like to get to know you better.

95
00:10:35,225 --> 00:10:38,745
So, can we interview you?

96
00:10:39,385 --> 00:10:41,785
-I'll ask the first question.
-Go ahead.

97
00:10:43,025 --> 00:10:46,025
Why did you choose
to study business administration?

98
00:10:46,105 --> 00:10:47,505
Jeez!

99
00:10:47,585 --> 00:10:49,425
That's such a formal question.

100
00:10:49,505 --> 00:10:51,625
Can you ask something more creative?

101
00:10:53,225 --> 00:10:54,185
I like this field,

102
00:10:54,785 --> 00:10:57,065
and I want to have
my own business someday.

103
00:10:57,705 --> 00:10:59,545
Jeez.

104
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:02,585
Next question.

105
00:11:03,505 --> 00:11:05,145
How many people have you dated?

106
00:11:05,785 --> 00:11:07,465
That's a bold question, dude.

107
00:11:18,865 --> 00:11:19,785
What is that?

108
00:11:20,385 --> 00:11:22,825
Zero. I've never been in a relationship.

109
00:11:22,905 --> 00:11:24,105
-What?
-Huh?

110
00:11:24,185 --> 00:11:27,385
Someone like you has never dated anyone?
That's hard to believe.

111
00:11:31,585 --> 00:11:32,905
Dig in.

112
00:11:45,265 --> 00:11:47,625
Well, I'm going to use the restroom.

113
00:11:57,145 --> 00:12:00,545
You and Rin are roommates.
Do you two ever fight?

114
00:12:00,625 --> 00:12:03,145
Do you take good care of Rin
when you're together?

115
00:12:03,225 --> 00:12:05,665
Has he ever been unreasonable with you?

116
00:12:17,025 --> 00:12:18,545
I have something to confess.

117
00:12:19,265 --> 00:12:20,625
I asked Rin if I could win him over.

118
00:12:24,185 --> 00:12:26,025
-What a surprise!
-Such a surprise!

119
00:12:26,105 --> 00:12:27,505
-Yeah.
-Actually…

120
00:12:28,105 --> 00:12:29,345
We already knew.

121
00:12:29,425 --> 00:12:31,705
-How did you know?
-How could we not?

122
00:12:31,785 --> 00:12:34,065
We've known from the start, dude.

123
00:12:38,985 --> 00:12:42,065
I’ll do everything I can for him.

124
00:12:42,145 --> 00:12:45,265
But if I ever make him uncomfortable,
I'll back off.

125
00:12:45,345 --> 00:12:46,785
-No way!
-No way!

126
00:12:46,865 --> 00:12:49,625
Don't you dare back off, Khobfa.

127
00:12:49,705 --> 00:12:52,145
Now that you've made your move,
there's no turning back.

128
00:12:52,225 --> 00:12:53,745
Exactly.

129
00:12:53,825 --> 00:12:57,025
If you have a problem with our friend
or don't understand him,

130
00:12:57,105 --> 00:12:59,545
just tell us and we'll coach you.

131
00:12:59,625 --> 00:13:01,625
Rin isn't that complicated.

132
00:13:01,705 --> 00:13:03,545
Just don't spoil him too much.

133
00:13:03,625 --> 00:13:04,705
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

134
00:13:05,585 --> 00:13:08,905
Since we're at it,
let's make a toast to Khobfa.

135
00:13:08,985 --> 00:13:11,265
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

136
00:13:11,345 --> 00:13:14,585
Hey. What are you toasting to?
Why didn't you wait for me?

137
00:13:14,665 --> 00:13:16,785
You're back! Come join the toast.

138
00:13:16,865 --> 00:13:18,145
-Come on. Cheers!
-Come on.

139
00:13:18,225 --> 00:13:21,145
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

140
00:13:31,265 --> 00:13:33,585
Do you want to talk?
It can be about anything.

141
00:13:33,665 --> 00:13:37,305
But it's okay if you don't want to.
I know that's just how you are.

142
00:13:37,385 --> 00:13:39,265
Do whatever you're comfortable with.

143
00:13:41,745 --> 00:13:43,585
So why do you like drawing?

144
00:13:44,185 --> 00:13:46,545
Wow. You're really asking me that?

145
00:13:47,225 --> 00:13:49,145
When I was little, I only drew for fun.

146
00:13:49,225 --> 00:13:51,945
Then someone saw my drawings
and said they were good.

147
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:56,945
That made me think I was good at it,
so I kept drawing.

148
00:13:57,025 --> 00:13:58,665
And I grew to love it.

149
00:13:59,705 --> 00:14:01,025
It's really nice, though.

150
00:14:01,105 --> 00:14:05,985
Whenever I feel something so strongly
that I can't put into words,

151
00:14:06,545 --> 00:14:08,065
I just draw it.

152
00:14:08,785 --> 00:14:12,385
It's like capturing that feeling
in a picture and preserving it.

153
00:14:24,665 --> 00:14:27,265
Hey. Sneaking a photo of me, huh?

154
00:14:28,465 --> 00:14:29,505
Let me see.

155
00:14:30,345 --> 00:14:31,425
Do I look good?

156
00:14:31,505 --> 00:14:32,945
Okay.

157
00:14:33,825 --> 00:14:36,105
Let's take a selfie
so we'll have a photo together.

158
00:14:43,025 --> 00:14:45,305
But it's okay if you're uncomfortable.

159
00:14:45,385 --> 00:14:47,985
No, I'm not uncomfortable.

160
00:14:48,065 --> 00:14:52,905
I've just never taken a selfie
with someone I'm hitting on before.

161
00:14:55,225 --> 00:14:57,705
Then I'm your first.

162
00:15:00,865 --> 00:15:03,505
Come on. You should practice
so you'll get used to it.

163
00:15:18,825 --> 00:15:20,145
Is something wrong?

164
00:15:20,745 --> 00:15:22,025
You're the one acting strange.

165
00:15:22,105 --> 00:15:25,385
You've been avoiding me
since we got back from Rayong

166
00:15:25,465 --> 00:15:26,825
and ignoring my messages.

167
00:15:27,425 --> 00:15:29,025
I've been busy with work lately.

168
00:15:30,705 --> 00:15:32,265
It's about that night, isn't it?

169
00:15:37,025 --> 00:15:40,865
You're avoiding me because of that night.

170
00:15:41,465 --> 00:15:43,425
What do you want me to do? Just tell me.

171
00:15:43,505 --> 00:15:45,105
Don't overthink it.

172
00:15:45,185 --> 00:15:46,945
We both had fun that night.

173
00:15:47,025 --> 00:15:50,665
That makes us even.
We don't owe each other anything.

174
00:15:50,745 --> 00:15:53,585
I have more work to do. I should go.

175
00:15:59,505 --> 00:16:01,105
Can I sleep in your room tonight?

176
00:16:06,505 --> 00:16:09,505
I think you should sleep
in your own room tonight.

177
00:16:20,745 --> 00:16:22,785
Hey, give me your phone.
I'll send it to myself.

178
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:26,545
There, done.

179
00:16:31,265 --> 00:16:32,665
Aren't you embarrassed

180
00:16:33,785 --> 00:16:35,585
to post me on your story?

181
00:16:36,545 --> 00:16:39,105
No. I set it to "close friends" only.

182
00:16:41,905 --> 00:16:43,625
There, it's posted.

183
00:16:45,745 --> 00:16:47,545
You added me to your "close friends"?

184
00:17:00,505 --> 00:17:02,185
Sneaky. You're being sneaky.

185
00:17:02,905 --> 00:17:03,985
Come on.

186
00:17:20,545 --> 00:17:22,865
Hey, what are you doing?

187
00:17:26,145 --> 00:17:28,825
From now on, you can sleep in my bed
whenever you want.

188
00:17:30,385 --> 00:17:31,265
What?

189
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:44,465
Are you uncomfortable?

190
00:17:45,145 --> 00:17:46,105
No.

191
00:17:47,265 --> 00:17:51,865
I just realized a king-sized bed
is perfect for two people.

192
00:18:06,785 --> 00:18:07,905
Ouch!

193
00:18:13,225 --> 00:18:14,385
Good night.

194
00:18:20,065 --> 00:18:21,785
I know you're secretly smiling.

195
00:18:23,225 --> 00:18:24,425
No, I'm not!

196
00:18:47,105 --> 00:18:52,065
From now on,
it's going to be just the two of us.

197
00:18:52,145 --> 00:18:54,545
Your dad has passed away.

198
00:18:58,945 --> 00:19:00,585
Don't accept it, Mom.

199
00:19:00,665 --> 00:19:01,905
Don't accept it, Mom.

200
00:19:01,985 --> 00:19:05,105
Our family has a mystical lineage.

201
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:06,305
If you choose to inherit it,

202
00:19:06,385 --> 00:19:08,785
-you must prepare to be unlucky in love.
-Don't accept it, Mom.

203
00:19:08,865 --> 00:19:10,185
Don't accept it, Mom.

204
00:19:10,265 --> 00:19:13,905
-Once you inherit it, if you fall in love,
-Please don't accept it.

205
00:19:13,985 --> 00:19:18,425
fate will take that person away from you.

206
00:19:27,305 --> 00:19:29,585
I'm not going to lose you too, am I?

207
00:19:35,665 --> 00:19:36,785
Is something wrong?

208
00:19:38,145 --> 00:19:39,825
I just had a little nightmare.

209
00:19:41,905 --> 00:19:45,425
I don't think these pillows

210
00:19:45,505 --> 00:19:47,785
are doing a very good job.

211
00:19:52,025 --> 00:19:55,425
So tonight, I'll be your pillow.

212
00:19:56,785 --> 00:19:58,465
Hug me instead.

213
00:20:00,705 --> 00:20:02,465
I'll hold you so tightly…

214
00:20:06,345 --> 00:20:07,945
that you can't go anywhere.

215
00:20:21,985 --> 00:20:23,025
All right, everyone.

216
00:20:23,105 --> 00:20:25,905
For your midterm assignment,

217
00:20:25,985 --> 00:20:31,345
I'd like you to create a drawing
based on the theme "A Painful Memory."

218
00:20:32,425 --> 00:20:34,545
Draw it however you like.

219
00:20:34,625 --> 00:20:38,705
Any style is fine,
as long as it fits the theme.

220
00:20:38,785 --> 00:20:44,585
If you fall in love,
fate will take that person away from you.

221
00:20:44,665 --> 00:20:45,705
Let's part ways.

222
00:20:45,785 --> 00:20:47,545
I don't think I can do this anymore.

223
00:20:55,465 --> 00:20:56,905
Look over there.

224
00:20:56,985 --> 00:20:58,865
Prof. James's star pupil.

225
00:20:58,945 --> 00:21:01,825
He looks ready to submit his work already.
Look at his face.

226
00:21:01,905 --> 00:21:04,825
Come on, Rin.
You came emotionally prepared, huh?

227
00:21:05,425 --> 00:21:06,905
Your head must be full of ideas.

228
00:21:07,905 --> 00:21:11,385
You're not the only one aiming for an A.
Share your ideas with us.

229
00:21:11,465 --> 00:21:13,185
Right. I can't think of anything.

230
00:21:30,745 --> 00:21:32,265
How is it going?

231
00:21:32,345 --> 00:21:34,025
Have you come up with anything?

232
00:21:36,665 --> 00:21:38,985
I've thought of a way to help you.

233
00:21:39,745 --> 00:21:43,425
First, slowly close your eyes

234
00:21:43,505 --> 00:21:45,985
and think of the saddest moment
in your life.

235
00:21:47,345 --> 00:21:49,345
Let your mind go wherever it takes you.

236
00:21:50,785 --> 00:21:53,745
Whatever you see first
is probably the one.

237
00:21:53,825 --> 00:21:57,665
-Don't accept it, Mom.
-Our family has a mystical lineage.

238
00:21:57,745 --> 00:22:01,185
If you choose to inherit it,
you must prepare to be unlucky in love.

239
00:22:01,265 --> 00:22:04,665
So you've been hiding
this whole mystical family thing from me?

240
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:08,665
No, Khobfa.

241
00:22:08,745 --> 00:22:09,665
No!

242
00:22:11,585 --> 00:22:13,105
Why did you hide it from me?

243
00:22:16,825 --> 00:22:18,665
You were afraid I wouldn't date you,
right?

244
00:22:19,625 --> 00:22:21,425
You were right.

245
00:22:21,505 --> 00:22:24,105
I'm already forcing myself
to stay with you.

246
00:22:25,425 --> 00:22:28,905
I regret ever trusting you.

247
00:22:32,465 --> 00:22:33,625
Get out!

248
00:22:34,905 --> 00:22:36,145
Khobfa!

249
00:22:36,225 --> 00:22:37,865
Please listen to me, Khobfa!

250
00:22:37,945 --> 00:22:40,345
Khobfa! Listen to me!

251
00:22:40,425 --> 00:22:42,785
Khobfa!

252
00:22:42,865 --> 00:22:43,825
Rin!

253
00:22:47,025 --> 00:22:48,105
Rin!

254
00:22:51,625 --> 00:22:53,345
It's ready. Let's eat.

255
00:23:00,585 --> 00:23:01,905
How are the noodles?

256
00:23:01,985 --> 00:23:04,105
They're my family's recipe. Are they good?

257
00:23:05,145 --> 00:23:06,945
Yeah, they're pretty good.

258
00:23:08,585 --> 00:23:11,265
If you like them,
I'll make them for you more often.

259
00:23:15,465 --> 00:23:18,465
By the way, what's wrong with you?

260
00:23:19,065 --> 00:23:21,945
You've been drawing for ages.
Is the assignment difficult?

261
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:24,545
Yeah, it is.

262
00:23:25,105 --> 00:23:26,705
The deadline is coming up too.

263
00:23:26,785 --> 00:23:29,145
I think I'll just make something
and submit it first.

264
00:23:29,225 --> 00:23:30,985
You'll come up with something soon.

265
00:23:32,385 --> 00:23:33,425
You're good at this.

266
00:23:34,505 --> 00:23:35,425
Thank you.

267
00:23:36,185 --> 00:23:38,385
Come on. Let's race to finish.

268
00:23:38,465 --> 00:23:40,465
-Come on.
-Let's start.

269
00:23:40,545 --> 00:23:43,145
Hey! You started before me!

270
00:23:43,745 --> 00:23:47,185
You ate the bacon! That's mine.
That piece of bacon is mine.

271
00:24:18,785 --> 00:24:20,065
You drew it well.

272
00:24:21,065 --> 00:24:22,945
It conveys the emotions excellently.

273
00:24:24,025 --> 00:24:25,625
Of course it does, Professor.

274
00:24:25,705 --> 00:24:28,665
She doesn't have a boyfriend.
They only got to the talking stage.

275
00:24:28,745 --> 00:24:30,985
-How pathetic.
-So what?

276
00:24:31,705 --> 00:24:33,585
I'm way more talented than you.

277
00:24:33,665 --> 00:24:34,825
Look at your piece.

278
00:24:34,905 --> 00:24:37,145
It belongs in the trash.

279
00:24:37,225 --> 00:24:39,385
-Ouch, that hurts!
-Next.

280
00:24:54,985 --> 00:24:58,025
Everyone, please wait outside.

281
00:24:58,865 --> 00:25:00,665
I'd like to speak with him alone.

282
00:25:20,585 --> 00:25:22,745
How does this painting
fit the theme I assigned?

283
00:25:23,545 --> 00:25:27,345
Well, for this piece,
I used a technique that--

284
00:25:27,425 --> 00:25:28,665
You don't have to answer.

285
00:25:30,185 --> 00:25:32,345
I think you already know, Rin.

286
00:25:32,425 --> 00:25:35,145
This painting feels like

287
00:25:35,225 --> 00:25:37,465
a forced interpretation
of "A Painful Memory."

288
00:25:38,905 --> 00:25:40,585
You're a talented artist.

289
00:25:41,385 --> 00:25:44,785
But if you can't accept pain
as part of life,

290
00:25:46,065 --> 00:25:48,425
you'll never make this piece work.

291
00:25:49,425 --> 00:25:51,065
I'm very disappointed in you.

292
00:25:51,625 --> 00:25:55,545
How can I nominate you
for the national competition like this?

293
00:25:55,625 --> 00:25:57,465
I'll give you until tomorrow.

294
00:25:58,425 --> 00:26:00,425
Redo it and submit it to me.

295
00:26:29,065 --> 00:26:30,065
Hello.

296
00:26:31,465 --> 00:26:33,665
Hello, Mom. Are you free to talk?

297
00:26:33,745 --> 00:26:35,745
Is something wrong, honey?

298
00:26:35,825 --> 00:26:37,145
You seem a little off.

299
00:26:38,305 --> 00:26:40,145
I haven't even said anything.

300
00:26:41,025 --> 00:26:43,345
How do you know I'm not okay?

301
00:26:44,185 --> 00:26:45,865
My intuition, I guess.

302
00:26:45,945 --> 00:26:49,905
Lately, your face keeps popping up
in my mind for no reason.

303
00:26:50,585 --> 00:26:54,305
What's wrong? Is something bothering you?

304
00:26:55,105 --> 00:26:56,105
Mom.

305
00:26:58,025 --> 00:27:00,345
When you inherited
our family's mystical gift,

306
00:27:00,425 --> 00:27:04,625
did you ever think you'd have to lose Dad?

307
00:27:09,705 --> 00:27:11,305
-Mom?
-Huh?

308
00:27:12,585 --> 00:27:14,625
I never thought about it that way.

309
00:27:15,585 --> 00:27:17,985
Your dad has been gone a long time.

310
00:27:18,065 --> 00:27:19,625
He's at peace now.

311
00:27:20,345 --> 00:27:22,985
Honestly, I don't really want
to talk about him.

312
00:27:24,865 --> 00:27:26,545
I'm afraid he'll worry about us.

313
00:27:26,625 --> 00:27:28,305
Do you think

314
00:27:30,225 --> 00:27:32,385
it was worth inheriting
that spiritual gift

315
00:27:33,465 --> 00:27:38,145
when it meant being unlucky in love,
just like you and Grandma?

316
00:27:44,145 --> 00:27:46,105
I have to go, honey.
Something just came up.

317
00:27:46,185 --> 00:27:48,385
Mom? Mom!

318
00:28:05,745 --> 00:28:07,305
Ohm, Jinnie.

319
00:28:07,385 --> 00:28:08,505
-Yeah?
-Yeah?

320
00:28:13,505 --> 00:28:16,385
Looking for Rin? He left.

321
00:28:17,265 --> 00:28:18,185
Yeah.

322
00:28:18,705 --> 00:28:23,225
Prof. James was really hard on him today,
so Rin asked to leave early.

323
00:28:23,305 --> 00:28:24,865
But we don't know where he went.

324
00:28:24,945 --> 00:28:27,145
Thanks. I'll try calling him.

325
00:28:27,225 --> 00:28:29,185
-Yeah, okay.
-Give it a try.

326
00:28:33,905 --> 00:28:37,665
Sorry, the number you have dialed
cannot be reached at this time.

327
00:28:37,745 --> 00:28:41,065
-Please leave a message.
-Well? Did he answer?

328
00:28:51,905 --> 00:28:53,025
Mochi!

329
00:28:59,305 --> 00:29:01,825
Sorry, the number you have dialed
cannot be reached…

330
00:29:09,425 --> 00:29:11,665
Mochi, don't do this.

331
00:29:11,745 --> 00:29:14,505
If something's wrong, talk to me.
Tell me what's going on.

332
00:29:14,585 --> 00:29:16,025
Don't disappear like this.

333
00:29:24,825 --> 00:29:27,385
Excuse me. Are you Mochi?

334
00:29:28,345 --> 00:29:30,345
-Yes.
-Can I take a selfie with you?

335
00:29:31,305 --> 00:29:32,705
Of course. I'd be happy to.

336
00:29:35,705 --> 00:29:36,825
I'm a huge fan.

337
00:29:36,905 --> 00:29:38,745
I follow both you and Krit.

338
00:29:39,265 --> 00:29:41,705
By the way, where's Krit?

339
00:29:43,705 --> 00:29:46,305
He's busy. I came here by myself.

340
00:29:48,025 --> 00:29:48,985
That's a pity.

341
00:29:49,065 --> 00:29:51,185
Thank you. Bye!

342
00:29:56,625 --> 00:29:59,585
That was so fake, Mochi.

343
00:30:02,425 --> 00:30:04,465
The world runs on appearances.

344
00:30:04,985 --> 00:30:06,665
Who wants to see us being sad?

345
00:30:18,665 --> 00:30:20,345
This drink's on me.

346
00:30:20,425 --> 00:30:22,625
You've been staring at that picture
for half an hour.

347
00:30:25,105 --> 00:30:28,665
So this is the reason
behind that stupid promise of yours?

348
00:30:28,745 --> 00:30:30,065
Seriously.

349
00:30:31,105 --> 00:30:32,585
Don't you feel anything for Krit?

350
00:30:36,305 --> 00:30:37,545
I don't know.

351
00:30:39,425 --> 00:30:41,425
I just don't want to break my promise.

352
00:30:41,505 --> 00:30:43,105
I don't want to be like Rin,

353
00:30:44,305 --> 00:30:47,025
who made his own rule
and then broke it himself.

354
00:30:48,145 --> 00:30:50,225
You're good at everything, Mochi.

355
00:30:50,305 --> 00:30:53,585
Why do you have to make things
so complicated and hurt yourself?

356
00:30:54,345 --> 00:30:55,785
I'll never understand.

357
00:31:16,985 --> 00:31:18,585
I'm very disappointed in you.

358
00:31:19,785 --> 00:31:22,665
-Don't accept it, Mom.
-If you can't accept pain as part of life,

359
00:31:22,745 --> 00:31:24,305
you'll never make this piece work.

360
00:31:24,385 --> 00:31:27,985
So you've been hiding
this whole mystical family thing from me?

361
00:31:28,065 --> 00:31:30,665
I regret ever trusting you.

362
00:31:44,385 --> 00:31:48,065
The security guard said Rin went back
to work at the faculty studio.

363
00:31:48,145 --> 00:31:49,505
Please check on him.

364
00:31:53,585 --> 00:31:55,145
Is no one else here?

365
00:31:55,225 --> 00:31:56,265
No.

366
00:31:56,345 --> 00:31:58,465
The last person who used the room said

367
00:31:58,545 --> 00:32:01,385
he was going to draw
on the rooftop of another building.

368
00:32:06,465 --> 00:32:07,385
Is it him?

369
00:32:07,465 --> 00:32:08,745
Yes.

370
00:32:09,865 --> 00:32:10,985
Thank you.

371
00:32:22,665 --> 00:32:24,585
I don't want to inherit
this mystical lineage!

372
00:32:24,665 --> 00:32:27,705
Do you hear me?
I don't want to be the next heir!

373
00:32:27,785 --> 00:32:30,585
I won't do it! I don't want it! I don't!

374
00:32:31,545 --> 00:32:35,865
Why do I have to be unlucky in love
just because I'm the heir?

375
00:32:36,545 --> 00:32:37,425
Hey!

376
00:32:39,025 --> 00:32:39,905
Rin!

377
00:32:53,465 --> 00:32:54,585
Khobfa.

378
00:33:18,345 --> 00:33:19,305
Here.

379
00:33:20,345 --> 00:33:21,585
I brought you some food.

380
00:33:22,665 --> 00:33:25,945
You haven't eaten anything, right?
Your stomach's growling.

381
00:33:29,705 --> 00:33:30,745
Thank you.

382
00:33:31,945 --> 00:33:32,985
Want to eat with me?

383
00:33:33,585 --> 00:33:34,745
You go ahead.

384
00:33:48,105 --> 00:33:49,505
You've got food all over your mouth.

385
00:33:50,025 --> 00:33:52,785
What? Where?

386
00:33:53,345 --> 00:33:54,265
Here?

387
00:34:15,824 --> 00:34:17,545
So what's going on?

388
00:34:18,985 --> 00:34:20,705
You can tell me anything.

389
00:34:21,344 --> 00:34:23,225
You don't have to keep it to yourself.

390
00:34:23,304 --> 00:34:25,505
You said we're in the talking stage.

391
00:34:27,185 --> 00:34:29,225
That means you can talk to me
about anything.

392
00:34:31,225 --> 00:34:35,824
This business bad boy named Khobfa
will protect you.

393
00:34:43,344 --> 00:34:44,264
Khobfa.

394
00:34:46,665 --> 00:34:49,905
I have a secret.

395
00:34:51,425 --> 00:34:52,945
If you find out,

396
00:34:54,225 --> 00:34:56,025
you might hate me.

397
00:35:10,465 --> 00:35:11,465
Where have you been?

398
00:35:11,545 --> 00:35:12,785
Just go home already.

399
00:35:14,545 --> 00:35:15,625
I'm not going anywhere.

400
00:35:16,225 --> 00:35:17,465
We need to talk.

401
00:35:26,065 --> 00:35:27,585
What else do you want, Krit?

402
00:35:27,665 --> 00:35:30,385
I'm already pretending
to date you to fool Rin.

403
00:35:30,465 --> 00:35:31,665
Aren't I?

404
00:35:31,745 --> 00:35:32,665
Don't worry.

405
00:35:32,745 --> 00:35:36,105
I have plenty of photos and videos
of us acting sweet together.

406
00:35:36,185 --> 00:35:37,705
I'll post them tonight. Are we done?

407
00:35:37,785 --> 00:35:39,145
I don't care about that.

408
00:35:40,465 --> 00:35:41,465
Then what do you care about?

409
00:35:51,025 --> 00:35:52,185
You, Mochi.

410
00:35:53,985 --> 00:35:54,985
I care about you.

411
00:36:00,185 --> 00:36:01,265
I missed you.

412
00:36:22,865 --> 00:36:24,865
Just tell me to stop

413
00:36:26,825 --> 00:36:28,065
and I will.

414
00:37:15,425 --> 00:37:20,785
I couldn't draw something
for Prof. James's "A Painful Memory" theme

415
00:37:21,625 --> 00:37:24,985
because there's a painful memory

416
00:37:25,065 --> 00:37:29,465
I've spent my whole life
running away from.

417
00:37:30,705 --> 00:37:34,025
What are you sad about? Can you tell me?

418
00:37:35,905 --> 00:37:37,505
Well…

419
00:37:38,545 --> 00:37:40,265
Our family has a mystical lineage.

420
00:37:41,825 --> 00:37:45,585
I know you may not be comfortable
with this sort of thing.

421
00:37:53,225 --> 00:37:55,385
But if I really have to become
the next heir,

422
00:37:56,865 --> 00:38:00,985
the consequences go far beyond that.

423
00:38:03,025 --> 00:38:06,625
In my family,
whoever inherits the mystical gift

424
00:38:07,225 --> 00:38:09,345
must pay the price
of being unlucky in love.

425
00:38:10,665 --> 00:38:12,385
On my last birthday,

426
00:38:12,465 --> 00:38:17,225
I felt a sign telling me
it was my turn to inherit it.

427
00:38:22,105 --> 00:38:24,145
When you asked if you could win me over,

428
00:38:25,385 --> 00:38:27,025
I was so happy.

429
00:38:28,225 --> 00:38:29,625
But part of me was afraid…

430
00:38:32,025 --> 00:38:35,465
I'd lose you because of my family's curse.

431
00:38:41,905 --> 00:38:43,385
It will be different with us.

432
00:38:43,465 --> 00:38:45,665
I'll never be like those people.

433
00:39:02,505 --> 00:39:06,145
I promise I'll never be like them.

434
00:39:14,145 --> 00:39:16,745
I've always worn this bracelet.

435
00:39:34,545 --> 00:39:36,585
I want you to look after it for me.

436
00:39:48,665 --> 00:39:51,145
This is my most treasured necklace.

437
00:39:52,825 --> 00:39:54,305
I've always worn it.

438
00:40:12,305 --> 00:40:14,465
I want you to look after mine too.

439
00:40:16,945 --> 00:40:17,785
Of course.

440
00:40:22,265 --> 00:40:24,385
Come on. Let's go back to our room.

441
00:41:06,785 --> 00:41:08,345
No matter what happens,

442
00:41:09,265 --> 00:41:11,905
remember that I'll always be by your side.

443
00:41:41,345 --> 00:41:46,345
If you can't accept pain as part of life,
you'll never make this piece work.

444
00:41:47,585 --> 00:41:49,065
Don't accept it, Mom.

445
00:41:49,145 --> 00:41:50,385
Please don't accept it.

446
00:41:50,465 --> 00:41:52,905
Your dad has been gone a long time.

447
00:41:52,985 --> 00:41:54,585
He's at peace now.

448
00:42:02,945 --> 00:42:04,465
Grandma, do you miss Grandpa?

449
00:42:08,185 --> 00:42:09,425
Here, Mom.

450
00:42:11,265 --> 00:42:14,385
I'm so proud of you, Rin.

451
00:42:16,985 --> 00:42:18,545
If your dad were still here,

452
00:42:19,865 --> 00:42:22,705
he would be just as proud.

453
00:42:22,785 --> 00:42:26,585
Once you inherit it, if you fall in love,

454
00:42:26,665 --> 00:42:32,865
-fate will take that person away from you.
-I promise I'll never be like them.

455
00:43:14,865 --> 00:43:16,665
I'm sorry for everything.

456
00:43:17,585 --> 00:43:19,625
Stop apologizing, Krit.

457
00:43:19,705 --> 00:43:22,425
No matter how many times you do it,
everything stays the same.

458
00:43:23,305 --> 00:43:25,185
But I really want to keep going with you.

459
00:43:27,105 --> 00:43:29,625
I want something more serious between us.

460
00:43:30,265 --> 00:43:35,545
Then let's meet halfway.

461
00:43:38,265 --> 00:43:40,225
From now on, let's be "F."

462
00:43:40,305 --> 00:43:41,465
Friends with benefits.

463
00:43:43,665 --> 00:43:46,185
-Can it be more than that?
-That's as far as I'll go.

464
00:43:49,625 --> 00:43:50,505
Okay.

465
00:43:52,425 --> 00:43:57,105
By the way, I listened
to the song you sent me.

466
00:43:57,185 --> 00:43:58,345
It was good.

467
00:43:58,425 --> 00:44:00,065
You can send me another one.

468
00:44:02,385 --> 00:44:03,225
You got it.

469
00:44:14,945 --> 00:44:18,825
Good luck, Rin. I'll be waiting
in our room to celebrate with you.

470
00:44:46,145 --> 00:44:48,385
How did it go? Did you pass?

471
00:45:06,745 --> 00:45:08,625
It's okay. You can try again.

472
00:45:09,825 --> 00:45:11,225
We'll figure it out together.

473
00:45:19,905 --> 00:45:21,785
Prof. James said…

474
00:45:25,905 --> 00:45:27,385
I passed.

475
00:45:30,785 --> 00:45:32,425
He said my work improved.

476
00:45:32,505 --> 00:45:35,305
It might not be the best piece,

477
00:45:36,385 --> 00:45:37,705
but I passed!

478
00:45:41,985 --> 00:45:43,345
You did so well.

479
00:45:51,505 --> 00:45:52,745
Thank you.

480
00:45:52,825 --> 00:45:56,905
I only made it through the difficult time
because of you.

481
00:45:57,985 --> 00:45:59,705
I didn't do anything.

482
00:46:00,825 --> 00:46:02,625
You're already good, Rin.

483
00:46:06,465 --> 00:46:07,545
You did.

484
00:46:08,985 --> 00:46:10,865
You stayed by my side.

485
00:46:22,625 --> 00:46:24,185
I think

486
00:46:28,185 --> 00:46:30,185
we can officially be
in the talking stage now.

487
00:46:32,905 --> 00:46:34,545
You don't need to win me over anymore.

488
00:46:36,785 --> 00:46:37,985
Really?

489
00:47:06,545 --> 00:47:08,545
-Surprise!
-Surprise!

490
00:47:08,625 --> 00:47:09,905
What are you two doing?

491
00:47:09,985 --> 00:47:11,225
Well, well.

492
00:47:11,305 --> 00:47:13,145
Why do you both look so flustered?

493
00:47:13,225 --> 00:47:14,545
Who's flustered?

494
00:47:14,625 --> 00:47:15,625
Come on.

495
00:47:15,705 --> 00:47:17,625
Let's celebrate Rin!

496
00:47:18,265 --> 00:47:19,585
Let's celebrate!

497
00:47:22,105 --> 00:47:24,025
We bought loads of snacks.

498
00:47:24,105 --> 00:47:25,625
-Let's see what you have.
-Wow.

499
00:47:25,705 --> 00:47:27,705
So many different things.

500
00:47:28,465 --> 00:47:29,665
What did you buy?

501
00:47:29,745 --> 00:47:31,105
Loads of stuff, dude.

502
00:47:31,185 --> 00:47:33,025
You like this one. You like this one.

503
00:47:33,105 --> 00:47:33,985
Yeah.

504
00:47:39,105 --> 00:47:42,825
Khobfa, come visit me this weekend, dear.

505
00:47:42,905 --> 00:47:45,185
-Grandma, I'm here!
-Come with me

506
00:47:45,265 --> 00:47:46,985
-Khobfa!
-to visit my grandma, okay?

507
00:47:47,665 --> 00:47:49,665
My dad called to remind me
about dinner at home.

508
00:47:49,745 --> 00:47:50,785
He told me to invite you.

509
00:47:50,865 --> 00:47:53,425
You're the first person
he's ever asked me to bring home.

510
00:47:57,785 --> 00:47:59,625
Come here. I'll take it off for you.

511
00:47:59,705 --> 00:48:01,025
Hey, no need.

512
00:48:01,105 --> 00:48:02,185
I can do it myself.

513
00:48:04,905 --> 00:48:05,985
Do you want to shower with me?

